<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Buellt</h1><p class="st-meta">450 CE – 900 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small Welsh kingdom around Builth Wells, ruled by a dynasty claiming descent from Vortigern, and later the place where Llywelyn ap Gruffudd was killed.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Buellt lay in the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-wye">Wye</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-irfon">Irfon</a> valleys around modern Builth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">Wells</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/historia-brittonum">Historia Brittonum</a> of about 829 says <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambrosius-aurelianus">Ambrosius</a> granted Buellt and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gwrtheyrnion">Gwrtheyrnion</a> to Pascent, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vortigern">Vortigern</a>, and names <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernmail">Fernmail</a> as the ruler of both in the author's own day. Among its wonders it lists Carn Cabal, a cairn said to bear the footprint of Arthur's hound.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is recorded of its government. It was a small upland kingdom of river valleys and hill grazing, generally ruled together with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gwrtheyrnion">Kingdom of Gwrtheyrnion</a> and lying between the larger realms of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-powys">Kingdom of Powys</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-brycheiniog">Kingdom of Brycheiniog</a> and the south-western kingdoms.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Buellt was absorbed by larger Welsh kingdoms in the 10th century and later became a cantref contested between Welsh princes and Norman lords, with a castle at Builth. In 1282 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a>, last native <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a>, was killed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilmeri">Cilmeri</a> in Buellt.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-buellt.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Buellt" width="320" height="339"><figcaption>Image: my work · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cantrefi.Medieval.Wales.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>450 CE – 900 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Fernmail</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Welsh</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Buellt, Builth</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=kingdom-of-buellt" aria-label="Kingdom of Buellt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4647 337 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Buellt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4967 593h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4967 593h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United Kingdom. <a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=kingdom-of-buellt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

